# V0/V1 supplied-material machine derivation

These modules are included in the scratch machine's selected executing-artifact
scope. They implement conditional local stage maps, not the complete request
or any production qualification. Earlier progress reports retain their original
source scope; only a fresh report covers this integration.

For one source small-VOLE vector, define `r_k=PRG(seed_k,iv,2^31+i)` with the
actual `ell_hat` bit truncation and zero byte padding. The source folds the
reordered list `r'_0=0`, `r'_j=r_(j xor hidden)` for j>0. Its level c output is
the XOR over odd positions at that level, hence exactly the XOR of r'_j whose
bit c is one. Changing variables k=j xor hidden gives

```
q_c = XOR_k (bit_c(k) XOR hidden_c) * r_k.
```

The omitted source seed k=hidden has coefficient zero in every column. It may
therefore be expanded by a charged concrete public AES circuit without changing
any output; no source seed is chosen by a secret address. This is not valid as
an uncharged or repeatable classical PRP challenge interaction.

`RowPRG` explicitly adds the tweak to IV's final little-endian32-bit word, and
the block counter to its first32-bit word, independently modulo2^32. It emits
all required AES blocks, selects the low `ell_hat` bits and zeroes byte padding.
Its clean response-XOR kernel uses the same supplied concrete AES construction.

`VectorFold` traverses every original seed, computes one clean row into shared
work, prepares each `bit_c(k) XOR hidden_c` flag, applies `ell_hat` controlled
XORs to each output column, clears all flags, and repeats RowPRG to clear the
row. After the scan it applies the source correction to the first ell bits of
each column selected by hidden_c. Vector0 has no correction input; c_0=0.
Tweak constants are prepared and cleared explicitly. Output columns are an
arbitrary XOR target, including padding bits that remain untouched.

For N=2^d and B=ceil(ell_hat/128), the per-vector clean cost is
`2N*cost(RowPRG)` plus `Nd*ell_hat + [i>0]*d*ell` Toffoli,
`2Nd` CNOT, and `Nd+2popcount(2^31+i)` X. The RowPRG clean cost already has2B
clean AES calls, so this vector has4NB concrete clean AES calls. It makes no
base-oracle calls. Work contains the padded row, RowPRG clean workspace, d flags
and32 tweak bits; every such bit returns to zero.

Four draft tests passed: independent source reordered-list/level-by-level fold
for all hidden indices at depths1..4, actual row truncation/word-wrap cases,
hidden-seed independence, and complete emitted-map counts/inverse/cleanup with
arbitrary output targets. These finite tests do not qualify the full V0 stage.

`mask_fold.py` now binds the exact two TREE_MODULI source arrays. Each source
bit j in column p contributes `x^(j+p) mod M_i` through explicit CNOTs. Only
the first d_i bits of each d0-bit mask window are read; output has source
64-bit word padding and source mask order0..9. Every actual selected basis wire
and image is checked independently for both tables.

`vole_columns.py` now composes every source vector, c_1..c_(tau-1) offsets and
typed u16 hidden-index slices. It computes the columns into retained zero
internal registers, computes shares into the caller target, copies columns,
then reverses every vector. Caller arbitrary column-target contents therefore
never contaminate shares. Exact clean cost is twice the sum of VectorFold
circuits plus the residue CNOT map plus one CNOT per output column bit. Work
is the retained full column matrix plus the maximum vector workspace.

The VoleColumns tests cover: every actual-table selected basis image/count,
refusal geometry, and full mixed-depth V0 emitted joint map/count/cleanup with
nonzero caller targets, compared with a mutable byte/polynomial source model.
Canonical mixed geometry is checked and copied into an owned immutable value;
mutating the original caller object cannot alter the subsequently emitted map.
B1-to-V0/full-request wiring remains outside this component.

## V1 and the clean joined map

Each selector/row lift is W_CRT. Each mask starts with W_TREE times its source
word-padded low share. Gate e has gamma_e=G[e] dot selector and label_e the XOR
of the first256 bits of the G[e]-selected columns. The H5 address is exactly
namespace77||IV16||salt32||e_u32_le||label32||domain5. The low ten response bits
are XORed with gamma_e*c_mult[m,e] before W_GATE is applied. Gate counts must
be byte aligned, as in both production rows (704 and696), so the correction
row stride is exactly the source ceil(g/8) bytes. No generic packed-bit stride
is silently equated with a different source byte layout.

The streamed circuit stores one label, gate counter, full query, full response,
ten-bit value and gamma. It reads the same immutable F twice to implement the
prefix-XOR call, applies correction and contribution, undoes correction, and
uses the same two-query prefix call to clear the value. It then clears frame,
label, gamma and counter. Total clean workspace is256+32+1296+2112+10+1=3707bits.
For matrix Hamming weights |W| its exact census is

```
X = 4g + 2*sum_e popcount(e)
CNOT = (ell+1)|W_CRT| + 10|W_TREE| + 514|G| + 2596g + 10|W_GATE|
Toffoli = 20g
F calls = 4g.
```

This includes both frame scatters and both prefix copies. It is a clean XOR
map for arbitrary caller Delta/Q/q_masks targets and does not retain a hidden
ordinary-oracle cache after return. Recomputing fixed F values preserves their
actual address correlations; it does not resample them. Source basis labels are
preserved, but their reduced state need not be unchanged when entangled with
the caller output. The circuit equality is on the joint registers.

The joined map retains V0's columns/shares, applies V1, then clears V0. It costs
2*V0+V1 and retains V0.output_bits+max(V0.work,3707) clean work bits. All other
input and output bits are separately inventoried. This uses a supplied valid
cross-stage relation: decoded hidden indices agree with the same selector;
the grinding tail is zero; seeds and corrections are matching source material.
B1-to-V0 wiring, public input validation, response/relation/log/return stages
and the whole-request public projection remain outstanding. No sum here is
claimed to be the complete simulator/reduction resource vector.
